---
id: weegloo-resource-deletion
type: rule
title: Weegloo resource deletion - dependency order and preconditions
description: >
  Deleting a Weegloo resource fails while a dependant still exists; nothing is force-deleted and
  nothing cascades upward. Space delete is blocked only by ContentType, Content, Media and
  WebHosting; ContentType is blocked by its Content; Published resources must be unpublished first.
  Before any teardown or on a 422 from a delete, invoke the weegloo-resource-deletion skill.
---

rules:
  - section: Critical invariants (always apply)
    items:
      - "**Deletes never cascade upward and nothing is force-deleted.** A parent is refused while a dependant exists — there is no `force` / `recursive` / `cascade` flag on any endpoint or MCP tool, and Weegloo will not delete a dependant for you. Teardown is therefore always **bottom-up**: delete the children yourself, one call each, then the parent. What the target *owns* (comments, snapshots, published projections, logs, storage objects, search views) is removed automatically once the delete is accepted — never delete those first, and never treat them as blockers."
      - "**Deleting a `Space` is blocked by EXACTLY four resource types, each `WGL422024`:** **`ContentType`**, **`Content`**, **`Media`**, **`WebHosting`**. Everything else in the Space **cascades** — `SpaceRole`, `SpaceMembership`, `Locale`, `Tag`, `Comment`, `ServiceLogin`, `ServiceUser`, `ServiceUserRole`, `Webhook` (+ logs/status), `Scheduler` (+ history), `Script` (+ logs), `DeliveryAccessToken`, `SpaceAccessToken` (with their synthetic users and cached credentials), `EmailAccount`, search UIs/views, the Space icon. **Do not delete those first** — the calls are wasted and can fail on their own preconditions for no reason."
      - "**`ContentType` requires that NO `Content` of it exists — any status (`WGL422010`).** `Draft` and `Archived` Content block it exactly like `Published` Content. ⚠️ **The same check also blocks `cma_UnpublishOneContentType`**, so a published ContentType with Content cannot be unpublished into a deletable state first — the order is forced: **delete every Content → unpublish the ContentType → delete it**. Recreating a ContentType to change a field therefore **destroys all its Content**; say so before proposing it."
      - "**`Content` / `ContentType` / `Media` delete only from `Draft` or `Archived` (`WGL422009`).** `Published` or `Changed` → **unpublish first** (`cma_UnpublishOneContent` / `…ContentType` / `…Media`), which needs the current `sys.version` in **`X-Weegloo-Version`**; **delete itself takes no version**. A **`Media` whose file is still `PENDING`/`PROCESSING`** (and a **`WebHosting`** mid-deploy) is refused with **`WGL422031`** — wait, do not retry in a loop."
      - "**`Archived` is NOT deleted.** An archived Content or Media is a live row that still blocks its Space and its ContentType. Archiving is not a teardown step, and archive is reachable only from `Draft` (`WGL422007`) — never a shortcut past an unpublish."
      - "**Nothing checks inbound references.** Deleting a `Content` or `Media` that another Content points at through a `Refer` field **succeeds** and leaves a dangling stub that expands to nothing on read (a missing image, an empty relation). Search for referrers first with `sys.contentType.sys.id=<CT>&fields.<refer>.<locale>.sys.id[eq]=<id>` — the `…/contents/{id}/references` endpoint answers the opposite question (what this Content points *to*)."
      - "**A `SpaceRole` that any access token is bound to cannot be deleted.** Every `DeliveryAccessToken` / `SpaceAccessToken` carries a hidden `SpaceMembership` on its synthetic user, so the role fails with **`WGL422024`** naming `SpaceMembership` with no human member in sight — and that membership cannot be deleted directly either (**`WGL422022`**, system-created user). **Delete the token**, not the membership."
      - "**Space and Organization deletes are gated by TOKEN TYPE, not only by role.** **`Space`** needs Organization **`ADMIN`** + `GLOBAL_SCOPE` → a **console login session or a Personal Access Token only**; a `SpaceAccessToken`, `DeliveryAccessToken`, ServiceUser token or Space-scoped console token cannot delete a Space whatever its bound role says — widening a `SpaceRole` never fixes it. **`Organization`** needs **`OWNER`** + `CONSOLE_SCOPE` → **console session only; a Personal Access Token cannot delete an Organization** (and it additionally requires the free plan, a settled subscription, and zero Spaces)."
      - "**Deleting is destructive and irreversible — confirm before deleting anything the user did not name**, and say what goes with it (a Space silently takes its roles, tokens, login configuration, scripts and schedulers). On a refusal, report the blocking resource in plain language, not the raw `WGL422…` code, and never resolve a `WGL422024` by deleting rows the user has not agreed to lose."

  - section: Full guidance
    items:
      - Per-resource preconditions (`Locale` default / last / `fallbackCode`, `ServiceUserRole`, `Script` used by a Webhook or Scheduler, `Tag`, `Organization` plan and subscription), the full Space teardown order, and the ACMA auto-unpublish contrast live in the **`weegloo-resource-deletion`** skill. Invoke it before any teardown and on any `WGL422…` from a delete. This rule is a safety-net summary, not a substitute.
